  "quiz_markdown": "### Q1. Dominant seventh contains a minor seventh above major triad.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q2. V7 resolves strongly to I.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q3. Major seventh is a half step below octave.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q4. Extensions are thirds stacked above the seventh.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q5. Triad is the core of tertian harmony.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q6. Jazz colour lesson expands triads further.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q7. Half-diminished is viiø7 in minor keys.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q8. Not every genre uses seventh chords equally.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q9. Advanced tier prepares secondary dominants.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q10. Added sixth is not the same as major seventh.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q11. Suspended chords replace third temporarily.\n\n**Answer:** True\n\n### Q12. Colour chords still resolve to tonic in tonal music.\n\n**Answer:** True",
